<%# Three lines, one of which always shows.

    Testing mode says so, always. A PLATFORM notice — the mail we write to the
    person who runs an account, never to their signers — is signed "Sent by
    EsignCenter": it is a statement of who sent the letter, and the
    free-document-signing line reads as an advertisement at the bottom of a
    bill reminder or a deletion notice. Everything else is the account's own
    mail to its signers, where the "Sent using" line is the product's
    marketing and is hidden only for an account entitled to branding removal
    that switched it on (Accounts.branding_removed?). With no account in
    scope, branding stays.

    None of these is the AGPL attribution; that lives in the interactive UI
    (shared/_powered_by, shared/_attribution) and is pinned by
    `rake gates:branding`. %>
<% if @current_account&.testing? %>
  <p>
    ---
  </p>
  <p>
    <%= t('sent_using_product_name_in_testing_mode_html', product_url: Docuseal::PRODUCT_EMAIL_URL, product_name: Docuseal.product_name) %>
  </p>
<% elsif platform_notice? %>
  <p>
    ---
  </p>
  <p>
    <%= t('sent_by_product_name_html', product_url: Docuseal::PRODUCT_EMAIL_URL, product_name: Docuseal.product_name) %>
  </p>
<% elsif !Accounts.branding_removed?(@current_account) %>
  <p>
    ---
  </p>
  <p>
    <%= t('sent_using_product_name_free_document_signing_html', product_url: Docuseal::PRODUCT_EMAIL_URL, product_name: Docuseal.product_name) %>
  </p>
<% end %>
